  "worked_solution": "At the point where $t=2$,  the vector ${r}^{\u2032}(2)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r(2)+u{r}^{\u2032}(2),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find $r(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =({2}^{2}-1)\\,i+\\sqrt{1+{2}^{2}}\\,j+(2-1)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i+\\sqrt{5}\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{\u2032}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}}\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ at $t=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(2) & =2(2)\\,i+\\frac{(2)}{\\sqrt{1+(2)^{2}}}\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =4\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point \n where $t=2$ is \n\n$$\nR(u)=3i+\\sqrt{5}\\,j+\\,k+u(4\\,i+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
